                    Compiling and Installing SLIM

PREPARATION
===========

A LMNtal compiler is needed to build SLIM. If it is not installed,
please install LMNtal compiler before building SLIM. You can download
LMNtal compiler from:
  https://www.ueda.info.waseda.ac.jp/lmntal/
  https://github.com/lmntal/lmntal-compiler

You must set the LMNTAL_HOME environment variable to the installed
directory of the LMNtal compiler.

REQUIREMENTS
============

- cmake 3.16+
- g++ or clang++
- re2c 1.0.3+
- bison 3.0+
- ruby 1.9.3+
- build-essential (on Ubuntu/Debian)

BASIC INSTALLATION
==================

The simplest way to compile this package is:

  1. Set the LMNTAL_HOME environment variable:
     export LMNTAL_HOME=/path/to/lmntal-compiler

  2. Run the build script:
     ./build-cmake.sh

  3. Optionally, run tests:
     ctest

  4. For system-wide installation:
     cd build
     sudo cmake --install . --prefix /usr/local

BUILD OPTIONS
=============

The build script supports the following options:

  ./build-cmake.sh --debug    # Debug build with debugging symbols
  ./build-cmake.sh --devel    # Developer mode with additional checks
  
You can also specify a custom build directory:
  ./build-cmake.sh --build-dir mybuild

TESTING
=======

To run tests:
  ctest                        # Basic tests
  ctest --output-on-failure   # Show detailed output on failures
  slim_CHECK_ND=yes ctest     # Include time-consuming model checking tests

MANUAL CMAKE BUILD
==================

If you prefer to use cmake directly:

  1. Create build directory:
     mkdir build && cd build

  2. Configure:
     cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release

  3. Build:
     make -j$(nproc)

  4. Test:
     ctest

  5. Install locally:
     make install

  6. Install system-wide:
     sudo cmake --install . --prefix /usr/local

CMAKE OPTIONS
=============

Available CMake options:
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release|Debug
  -DENABLE_DEBUG=ON|OFF        # Enable debug features
  -DENABLE_DEVEL=ON|OFF        # Enable developer features
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=path  # Installation directory

USAGE
=====

After installation, SLIM binaries are available:
  - Local build: ./build/bin/slim
  - System-wide: slim (if installed to /usr/local/bin)

For more information, see README.md